00:03:15,994 --> 00:03:20,974
Chaos Theory

420
00:03:15,994 --> 00:03:20,974
Homeostasis

421
00:03:40,594 --> 00:03:41,304
Daru?

422
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:44,104
No record in the outbox...

423
00:03:44,564 --> 00:03:47,604
But as for the inbox, 
the D-mail arrived five days ago.

424
00:03:47,604 --> 00:03:48,934
It succeeded.

425
00:03:48,934 --> 00:03:50,524
Did the past change?

426
00:03:51,354 --> 00:03:53,524
Why do you remember that?

427
00:03:59,204 --> 00:04:01,994
<i>We sent a D-mail to Daru five days in the past,</i>

428
00:04:02,414 --> 00:04:05,244
<i>telling him the position of the cards,</i>

429
00:04:05,244 --> 00:04:07,294
<i>so he could win the Feyris Cup.</i>

430
00:04:07,954 --> 00:04:09,084
Mayushii?

431
00:04:09,414 --> 00:04:13,334
Question for you... In the Feyris Cup last week...

432
00:04:13,334 --> 00:04:16,464
What? I lost? Immediately?

433
00:04:16,884 --> 00:04:20,304
I see... Thanks. Bye.

434
00:04:25,474 --> 00:04:28,814
Daru's message didn't alter the past.

435
00:04:29,774 --> 00:04:32,394
With the way the game went, 
it should have changed.

436
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:36,404
It wasn't enough to change world lines.

437
00:04:36,694 --> 00:04:39,154
Then we need an easier way to tell

438
00:04:39,154 --> 00:04:41,324
if the past has changed.

439
00:04:44,164 --> 00:04:48,124
I-It still isn't like I agree with 
these experiments, okay?

440
00:04:48,794 --> 00:04:50,914
So... What do you think?

441
00:04:51,334 --> 00:04:54,084
About you being the only one to remember?

442
00:04:54,384 --> 00:04:55,424
I told you.

443
00:04:55,424 --> 00:04:58,924
It's the power of the magic eye, Reading Steiner!

444
00:05:01,174 --> 00:05:03,304
In order to see if that's true,

445
00:05:03,304 --> 00:05:05,684
I'll have you send the next D-mail.

446
00:05:07,474 --> 00:05:09,064
I don't want to.

447
00:05:09,424 --> 00:05:11,524
Worried about a time paradox?

448
00:05:12,394 --> 00:05:16,274
It feels unfair to change the past.

449
00:05:18,984 --> 00:05:23,284
I've only lived eighteen years, 
but I don't want to change any of them.

450
00:05:23,714 --> 00:05:26,994
They're all part of my life, even the failures.

451
00:05:26,994 --> 00:05:31,124
But you love experiments, right?

452
00:05:31,544 --> 00:05:33,004
I-Is that wrong?

453
00:05:33,004 --> 00:05:36,174
In other words, you'll just sit back and watch,

454
00:05:36,174 --> 00:05:38,464
as others sacrifice themselves.

455
00:05:38,464 --> 00:05:40,674
A true mad scientist.

456
00:05:41,134 --> 00:05:42,594
Enough!

457
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:44,804
But seriously...

458
00:05:47,234 --> 00:05:50,664
Please

459
00:05:47,234 --> 00:05:50,664
I want to send a D-mail too!
Moeka

460
00:05:51,144 --> 00:05:54,354
But seriously... 
If we're going to perfect the D-mail...

461
00:05:55,654 --> 00:05:57,834
Please?

462
00:05:55,654 --> 00:05:57,834
It's okay, right? 
Please! 
Moeka

463
00:05:59,484 --> 00:06:01,654
