464
00:06:02,244 --> 00:06:04,554
I'm...

465
00:06:02,244 --> 00:06:04,554
A lab member, too, right? 
Moeka

466
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:03,744
Kiryuu-san?

467
00:06:04,454 --> 00:06:05,534
Enough!

468
00:06:05,954 --> 00:06:06,614
I can't?

469
00:06:16,254 --> 00:06:18,924
She overwhelmed us...

470
00:06:22,094 --> 00:06:25,224
Okay, we're here!

471
00:06:25,934 --> 00:06:27,184
Those crÃªpes were good...

472
00:06:27,184 --> 00:06:28,094
Yeah.

473
00:06:29,974 --> 00:06:32,064
Hey! You look bored.

474
00:06:32,064 --> 00:06:34,024
I'm waiting for someone.

475
00:06:34,604 --> 00:06:37,564
Hey, don't scare Nae!

476
00:06:37,564 --> 00:06:39,194
I didn't do anything!

477
00:06:39,594 --> 00:06:40,904
Come on, Nae.

478
00:06:40,904 --> 00:06:44,404
Let's leave this loser alone and go inside.

479
00:06:45,574 --> 00:06:46,824
Hi!

480
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:49,704
Mayuri-oneechan!

481
00:06:53,664 --> 00:06:55,044
I'll give this to you.

482
00:06:55,504 --> 00:06:56,624
Thanks!

483
00:06:58,624 --> 00:07:00,214
Here's one for Okarin, too!

484
00:07:06,304 --> 00:07:08,514
Yo!

485
00:07:08,874 --> 00:07:10,554
Good morning, Suzu-san.

486
00:07:10,554 --> 00:07:11,804
It's the part-timer girl!

487
00:07:12,304 --> 00:07:16,394
Hey... What happened after that?

488
00:07:16,394 --> 00:07:17,314
With what?

489
00:07:17,314 --> 00:07:19,194
The time machine!

490
00:07:19,194 --> 00:07:20,904
Did you ask John Titor?

491
00:07:20,904 --> 00:07:25,444
Yeah, but I don't know if 
what he says is accurate...

492
00:07:27,154 --> 00:07:28,404
Which part?

493
00:07:29,364 --> 00:07:31,414
Why are you so interested?

494
00:07:32,324 --> 00:07:35,294
You're a Titor otaku, aren't you?

495
00:07:35,294 --> 00:07:36,504
No.

496
00:07:36,504 --> 00:07:37,964
Kurisu-chan!

497
00:07:39,254 --> 00:07:40,424
Good morning.

498
00:07:52,644 --> 00:07:55,264
More sparks between you two?

499
00:07:55,264 --> 00:07:56,644
What's her problem, anyway?

500
00:07:57,524 --> 00:07:59,604
Fighting makes me sad.

501
00:08:00,444 --> 00:08:02,234
Don't worry! It's okay.

502
00:08:03,444 --> 00:08:04,484
Thank you.

503
00:08:04,854 --> 00:08:06,694
No private messages.

504
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:09,114
We want something simple, that will make it clear

505
00:08:09,114 --> 00:08:11,204
whether the past's changed.

506
00:08:15,164 --> 00:08:18,584
"I changed my cell phone four days ago,

507
00:08:18,584 --> 00:08:22,124
and I want to tell myself not to do it."

508
00:08:22,424 --> 00:08:23,714
I see.

509
00:08:23,714 --> 00:08:27,094
So if the past changes, 
you'll have a different cell phone.

510
00:08:27,504 --> 00:08:28,464
It would be obvious.

511
00:08:29,094 --> 00:08:31,434
Then let us begin the experiment!

512
00:08:42,024 --> 00:08:45,614
Right! Activate the Phone Microwave 
(name subject to change)!

513
00:08:48,574 --> 00:08:50,654
It's so round...

514
00:08:50,654 --> 00:08:51,404
What is this?

515
00:08:52,914 --> 00:08:57,494
I used the wrong number for 
the Lotto-6 you asked me about.

516
00:08:57,494 --> 00:08:58,664
This is my apology.

517
00:08:58,994 --> 00:09:02,164
I... I see.

518
00:09:03,044 --> 00:09:05,214
Good... Good to hear!

519
00:09:05,214 --> 00:09:07,884
The day nears, when your heart's eye will open.

520
00:09:07,884 --> 00:09:08,964
Yes!

521
00:09:08,964 --> 00:09:10,134
Excuse me, then.

522
00:09:10,854 --> 00:09:11,924
You're leaving?

523
00:09:12,264 --> 00:09:14,934
You seem busy.

524
00:09:16,484 --> 00:09:17,764
Goodbye.

525
00:09:19,014 --> 00:09:21,934
Wear Mayushii's cosplay sometime soon, okay?

526
00:09:21,934 --> 00:09:23,524
I-I'm sorry.

527
00:09:23,524 --> 00:09:25,274
I'm not really into that...

528
00:09:25,274 --> 00:09:26,814
So you won't?

529
00:09:26,814 --> 00:09:28,864
I think you'd look great...

530
00:09:29,514 --> 00:09:30,614
Goodbye.

531
00:09:31,694 --> 00:09:33,154
Bye-bye!

532
00:09:35,784 --> 00:09:37,124
Good kid, huh?

533
00:09:37,124 --> 00:09:38,204
Yeah.

534
00:10:02,814 --> 00:10:04,984
<i>This feeling again.</i>

535
00:10:05,444 --> 00:10:06,444
<i>Which means...</i>

536
00:10:07,904 --> 00:10:10,324
<i>The past changed?</i>

537
00:10:21,244 --> 00:10:23,664
Wh-Where's Shining Finger?

538
00:10:24,164 --> 00:10:25,164
Shi...

539
00:10:26,154 --> 00:10:27,334
Japanese... Do you speak it?

540
00:10:38,414 --> 00:10:41,184
Rukako didn't stop by?

541
00:10:41,184 --> 00:10:44,314
Rukako? Nope.

542
00:10:44,314 --> 00:10:47,274
Then, Moeka... Where's Moeka?

543
00:10:47,274 --> 00:10:49,354
Moeka-san? Who's that?

544
00:10:50,864 --> 00:10:52,574
Kiryuu Moeka!

545
00:10:52,574 --> 00:10:54,234
She wasn't here today?

546
00:10:54,234 --> 00:10:55,284
Well?

547
00:10:56,534 --> 00:10:57,454
Who's that?

548
00:11:00,164 --> 00:11:03,914
Kiryuu Moeka... I've never heard that name.

549
00:11:04,224 --> 00:11:05,374
What?

550
00:11:06,164 --> 00:11:08,254
Another D-mail?

551
00:11:08,674 --> 00:11:10,384
Wh-What do you mean?

552
00:11:10,964 --> 00:11:16,554
The past changed, 
and Moeka's very existence disappeared?

553
00:11:16,554 --> 00:11:17,724
Impossible!

554
00:11:18,884 --> 00:11:23,684
Up to July 31st, my inbox still has messages from her.

555
00:11:34,364 --> 00:11:35,654
"Something wrong?"

556
00:11:35,654 --> 00:11:37,744
"Sorry, I'm kind of busy."

557
00:11:37,744 --> 00:11:39,324
"I'll message you later."

558
00:11:43,744 --> 00:11:45,414
In other words,

559
00:11:45,414 --> 00:11:49,124
the past altered in such a way that, 
ever since four days ago,

560
00:11:49,124 --> 00:11:51,334
when she received that message,

561
00:11:51,334 --> 00:11:53,094
this Kiryuu... Moeka-san

562
00:11:53,094 --> 00:11:55,214
changed her actions and never came to the lab.

563
00:11:55,754 --> 00:11:57,594
I suppose so.

564
00:11:59,344 --> 00:12:02,514
And this time, only you remember it.

565
00:12:02,514 --> 00:12:05,724
The Reading Steiner, was it?

566
00:12:06,144 --> 00:12:08,684
By the way, just saying that embarrasses me.

567
00:12:08,684 --> 00:12:10,314
I don't think you should call it that.

568
00:12:10,734 --> 00:12:14,314
I'm not interested in your personal opinion.

569
00:12:15,524 --> 00:12:18,864
The power to maintain memories across world lines.

570
00:12:19,324 --> 00:12:21,824
Is it real?

571
00:12:23,954 --> 00:12:25,704
Here I am!

572
00:12:27,914 --> 00:12:29,374
We'll talk tomorrow.

573
00:12:30,794 --> 00:12:33,044
See you tomorrow, Okarin!

574
00:12:35,424 --> 00:12:37,254
<i>I really do have that ability.</i>

575
00:12:37,384 --> 00:12:40,144
I want you to be the messiah.

576
00:12:38,594 --> 00:12:39,594
<i>That means...</i>

577
00:12:40,884 --> 00:12:41,884
<i>I...</i>

578
00:12:45,644 --> 00:12:49,564
I'm amazed they can sleep at the lab...

579
00:12:49,564 --> 00:12:52,064
He said it's 'cause he's a mad scientist.

580
00:12:52,524 --> 00:12:56,064
I know! Let's all sleep over at the lab!

581
00:12:56,404 --> 00:12:58,234
If the guys aren't there.

582
00:12:58,234 --> 00:13:00,824
I know, why not come to my hotel?

583
00:13:01,154 --> 00:13:02,154
Could I?

584
00:13:02,444 --> 00:13:03,574
Of course.

585
00:13:03,574 --> 00:13:04,114
Sure!

586
00:13:04,624 --> 00:13:06,204
Okay, I'll come over soon!

587
00:13:10,754 --> 00:13:11,754
Ruka-kun?

588
00:13:13,754 --> 00:13:14,504
Yeah...

589
00:13:14,504 --> 00:13:16,384
Yeah... What?!

590
00:13:16,924 --> 00:13:18,344
Really?

591
00:13:19,844 --> 00:13:21,554
What?!

592
00:13:21,554 --> 00:13:24,514
You didn't bring the Magic Blade Samidare?

593
00:13:24,514 --> 00:13:24,894
Um...

594
00:13:24,894 --> 00:13:26,264
Don't say that, Okarin!

595
00:13:26,684 --> 00:13:30,434
Today, Ruka-kun is my guest.

596
00:13:30,434 --> 00:13:32,934
He's going to wear my cosplay!

597
00:13:32,934 --> 00:13:34,654
Um... I...

598
00:13:34,654 --> 00:13:38,904
Come on. Let's transform, Ruka-kun. Transform!

599
00:13:38,904 --> 00:13:40,734
Um, I mean, I...

600
00:13:41,284 --> 00:13:43,824
Let's take off your clothes...

601
00:13:43,824 --> 00:13:45,864
No, don't touch me there!

602
00:13:46,574 --> 00:13:47,454
Okay!

603
00:13:47,454 --> 00:13:48,914
I'll put it on myself!

604
00:13:48,914 --> 00:13:50,334
So leave me alone.

605
00:13:50,334 --> 00:13:53,214
You have to know the trick to putting this on.

606
00:13:53,214 --> 00:13:56,334
P-Please... Don't take off my clothes!

607
00:13:56,334 --> 00:13:59,004
This is very yuri.

608
00:13:59,004 --> 00:14:02,174
No. Rukako is a guy.

609
00:14:02,174 --> 00:14:03,844
Which means...

610
00:14:04,264 --> 00:14:05,804
It's even better!

611
00:14:12,724 --> 00:14:15,144
It's Kirari-chan from Rai-Net.

612
00:14:17,944 --> 00:14:20,694
You're as cute as I imagined, Ruka-kun!

613
00:14:20,694 --> 00:14:23,244
This is really embarrassing...

614
00:14:23,244 --> 00:14:24,654
It's okay!

615
00:14:24,654 --> 00:14:26,534
Cute is justice.

616
00:14:26,874 --> 00:14:29,374
I want to get a low-angle shot of this.

617
00:14:29,664 --> 00:14:31,284
What do you think, Okarin?

618
00:14:32,294 --> 00:14:33,414
That's right...

619
00:14:36,154 --> 00:14:37,084
It's me!

620
00:14:37,084 --> 00:14:39,884
I've just been victimized by a 
fierce psychological attack!

621
00:14:39,884 --> 00:14:40,924
This is bad!

622
00:14:40,924 --> 00:14:43,094
My soul... My soul is being devoured!

623
00:14:44,014 --> 00:14:46,844
Wh-What's wrong, Kyouma-san?

624
00:14:46,844 --> 00:14:49,264
What's with him?

625
00:14:49,684 --> 00:14:50,644
Kurisu-chan!

626
00:14:56,984 --> 00:15:01,064
Stop staring, pervert assistant.

627
00:15:01,504 --> 00:15:02,614
I'm not staring!

628
00:15:02,904 --> 00:15:04,864
Further win!

629
00:15:05,174 --> 00:15:06,614
What do you think of this cosplay?

630
00:15:06,614 --> 00:15:08,204
Does it look good?

631
00:15:08,824 --> 00:15:10,574
Yes... It's very cute.

632
00:15:10,914 --> 00:15:13,704
C-Cute... Well, I...

633
00:15:13,704 --> 00:15:15,834
Let's try on the others!

634
00:15:16,714 --> 00:15:17,964
Wait!

635
00:15:17,964 --> 00:15:24,054
I came here because I had a request for you.

636
00:15:24,054 --> 00:15:27,134
You didn't come here to wear my cosplay?

637
00:15:27,134 --> 00:15:31,554
I-I said no. But you wouldn't listen to me...

638
00:15:32,134 --> 00:15:34,064
I'm sorry. I was just really happy.

639
00:15:34,064 --> 00:15:35,894
So what did you want to ask?

640
00:15:36,204 --> 00:15:37,734
Actually...

641
00:15:39,984 --> 00:15:42,814
I want you to let me send a message to the past!

642
00:15:43,944 --> 00:15:45,074
I came by...

643
00:15:47,244 --> 00:15:52,414
...to apologize for having missed
the Lotto-6 yesterday. And then...

644
00:15:53,074 --> 00:15:54,994
<i>Another D-mail?</i>

645
00:15:54,994 --> 00:15:57,704
<i>Wh-What do you mean?</i>

646
00:15:57,704 --> 00:16:03,044
<i>The past changed, and Moeka's very existence disappeared?</i>

647
00:16:04,004 --> 00:16:05,004
<i>Impossible!</i>

648
00:16:05,524 --> 00:16:08,514
I'm sorry for listening when I shouldn't have!

649
00:16:08,514 --> 00:16:10,184
I didn't mean to!

650
00:16:11,144 --> 00:16:14,894
Ruka-kun, what kind of message 
do you want to send to the past?

651
00:16:15,334 --> 00:16:17,144
Actually, I...

652
00:16:18,954 --> 00:16:20,604
I want to be a girl!

653
00:16:23,904 --> 00:16:28,154
I don't like the way I look.

654
00:16:28,154 --> 00:16:32,534
I think I'd feel better about myself 
if I could be a girl...

655
00:16:32,534 --> 00:16:34,994
I've always felt that way.

656
00:16:35,404 --> 00:16:38,794
W-Wait a second...

657
00:16:38,794 --> 00:16:41,924
What is she saying?

658
00:16:42,624 --> 00:16:47,554
Assistant, you appear to have 
made a fatal mistake.

659
00:16:47,554 --> 00:16:48,384
Mistake?

660
00:16:49,094 --> 00:16:50,724
Rukako is no girl.

661
00:16:51,164 --> 00:16:51,844
He's a guy.

662
00:16:52,134 --> 00:16:54,434
What kind of joke is that?

663
00:16:54,434 --> 00:16:55,804
You don't believe me...

664
00:16:55,804 --> 00:16:59,474
If you call yourself a scientist, 
then see for yourself.

665
00:17:04,354 --> 00:17:07,904
Such a cute girl couldn't be a guy.

666
00:17:08,734 --> 00:17:10,114
Excuse me for a second.

667
00:17:16,974 --> 00:17:18,414
Are you okay?

668
00:17:19,204 --> 00:17:21,254
I'm serious!

669
00:17:21,254 --> 00:17:23,674
I really want to be a girl!

670
00:17:24,064 --> 00:17:25,544
Please!

671
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:28,634
But I don't know if sending a D-mail

672
00:17:28,634 --> 00:17:31,214
would be enough to change your gender.

673
00:17:31,534 --> 00:17:33,094
I heard of something...

674
00:17:33,094 --> 00:17:36,644
That if you eat lots of meat 
when a baby is in your tummy,

675
00:17:36,644 --> 00:17:37,604
you'll have a boy.

676
00:17:37,604 --> 00:17:40,854
With a lot of vegetables, you'll have a girl.

677
00:17:42,524 --> 00:17:45,064
You want us to send a D-mail, telling your mom

678
00:17:45,064 --> 00:17:46,654
to eat lots of vegetables?

679
00:17:46,654 --> 00:17:48,524
Would that be possible?

680
00:17:48,524 --> 00:17:49,774
Very well.

681
00:17:49,774 --> 00:17:51,654
I shall grant your wish.

682
00:17:52,404 --> 00:17:54,114
Thank you!

683
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:56,164
Good for you, Ruka-kun!

684
00:17:56,164 --> 00:17:57,164
Yes!

685
00:17:57,164 --> 00:18:00,244
Isn't changing someone's gender a bad idea?

686
00:18:00,244 --> 00:18:02,124
Do you think it's possible to affect it,

687
00:18:02,124 --> 00:18:04,374
just by eating vegetables?

688
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:05,464
That's true.

689
00:18:05,464 --> 00:18:07,834
There's no scientific evidence for it.

690
00:18:07,834 --> 00:18:09,924
He must have really been worried about it

691
00:18:09,924 --> 00:18:11,714
if that makes him feel better.

692
00:18:12,434 --> 00:18:18,094
Rukako, from now on, you're Lab Member 006!

693
00:18:18,094 --> 00:18:19,264
Y-Yes.

694
00:18:19,264 --> 00:18:21,434
Let us begin the experiment...

695
00:18:22,024 --> 00:18:24,434
Wait, you're seventeen this year, right?

696
00:18:24,434 --> 00:18:26,024
Huh? Yes.

697
00:18:26,024 --> 00:18:29,444
In other words, you were born in 1993...

698
00:18:29,864 --> 00:18:31,404
What of it?

699
00:18:31,704 --> 00:18:35,744
When did cell phones become popular in Japan?

700
00:18:39,204 --> 00:18:42,164
It looks like it was around 1996.

701
00:18:42,164 --> 00:18:44,964
And they may only later have 
gotten messaging capability.

702
00:18:44,964 --> 00:18:47,674
In other words, when Urushibara-san was born,

703
00:18:47,674 --> 00:18:51,094
there's a good chance his mom 
didn't own a cell phone.

704
00:18:51,094 --> 00:18:53,764
Then we can't send the D-mail?

705
00:18:53,764 --> 00:18:54,594
Oh, no.

706
00:18:55,384 --> 00:18:58,304
We could change it, so it sends sinister microwaves.

707
00:18:58,304 --> 00:19:00,854
You have enough sinister microwaves for everyone.

708
00:19:00,394 --> 00:19:03,814
Good... Insult me more.

709
00:19:03,814 --> 00:19:05,684
That's fine...

710
00:19:06,154 --> 00:19:07,524
I see.

711
00:19:10,114 --> 00:19:12,114
I'm terrified by my own talent!

712
00:19:12,114 --> 00:19:13,574
Not this again...

713
00:19:14,074 --> 00:19:17,704
If she doesn't have a cell phone, 
send it to her pager!

714
00:19:17,704 --> 00:19:18,954
Pagers...

715
00:19:18,954 --> 00:19:22,374
A system using EM waves to 
transmit messages to small receivers.

716
00:19:22,784 --> 00:19:25,794
During the 1990s, 
they enjoyed enormous popularity.

717
00:19:26,334 --> 00:19:28,794
The emergence of cellular phones 
rendered them obsolete.

718
00:19:29,324 --> 00:19:30,424
Pagers?

719
00:19:30,424 --> 00:19:32,344
I've never seen one!

720
00:19:32,344 --> 00:19:33,384
You're very knowledgeable.

721
00:19:33,384 --> 00:19:35,304
I guess you were a Cel-Pager, not a Cel-7?

722
00:19:35,304 --> 00:19:36,674
It's written right there.

723
00:19:36,674 --> 00:19:37,974
Why not read it yourself?

724
00:19:40,474 --> 00:19:43,474
Lab Member 006, Urushibara Ruka!

725
00:19:43,474 --> 00:19:44,564
It's time for your first mission.

726
00:19:45,254 --> 00:19:47,434
Find out if your mother had a pager.

727
00:19:47,434 --> 00:19:49,064
And get that number!

728
00:19:49,064 --> 00:19:50,444
Y-Yes, sir!

